<article class="env-lemma" id="0FV8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FV8">Lemma <span data-tag="0FV8">42.56.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. There is a ring map $\psi ^{-1} : K_0(\textit{Vect}(X)) \to K_0(\textit{Vect}(X))$ which sends $[\mathcal{E}]$ to $[\mathcal{E}^\vee ]$ when $\mathcal{E}$ is finite locally free and is compatible with pullbacks. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The only thing to check is that taking duals is compatible with short exact sequences and with pullbacks. This is clear. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>